    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Status of Implementation Progress: 1. (Phase 1) Installation of solar photovoltaic generators and connection to the existing distribution networks (200 kWp on Eua, SCADA repair program on Vava&apos;u and 550 kWp on Haapai with 330 kWp of batteries) completed.

(Phase 2) Installation of 6.5 kWh of batteries across 130 solar home systems on Niuafoou; a new solar system for the Health Clinic and 160 kWp solar home systems on Niuafoou; installation of solar photovoltaic generators and connection to the existing community-owned and -managed electrical mini-grids on 4 Haapai outer islands (100 kWp of solar and 210 kWh of batteries on Uiha, 100 kWp of solar and 210 kWh of batteries on Nomuka, 100 kWp of solar and 210 kWh of batteries on Haano, 60 kWp of solar and 110 kWh of batteries on Haafeva) and on Niuatoputapu (150kWp of solar and 295 kWh of batteries) completed.

(Phase 3): 100% rehabilitation of existing grid network on Eua completed and TPL will complete 100% rehabilitation of existing grid network on Vavau (includes new households) by Apr24.

(Phase 4): The upgrade of the existing service lines on 4 Haapai outer islands (Haano, Uiha, Haafeva and Nomuka) and the construction of a new mini grid on Niuatoputapu have been completed.

2. O&amp;M consultant recruited in Mar21 to examine the transfer of the 5 project mini grids, from the existing MEIDECC society setup to the TPL Concessions contract. The consultant&apos;s scope of work included the setting up, direction, coordination, control, execution, reporting, successful implementation and completion of the project O&amp;M plan. The consultant&apos;s work included tariff modeling of the following scenarios (a) covering OPEX only and managed by the ECOS; (b) covering OPEX and replacement (each island at their own tariff managed by the ECOS; (c) covering one tariff OPEX and replacement across the 5 mini-grids (ECOS to manage their respective islands); and (d) TPL transfer (equates to a 2 sene increase in the overall tariff). The O&amp;M Consultant produced the 8 required reports. In July 2023, TPL responded to MEIDECC agreeing, in principle, to handle the O&amp;M of the 5 mini grids. MEIDECC will support the ECOS until the 5 mini grids are included in TPL&apos;s next Concession Contract in June 2025.

3. A project management consultant firm was recruited in Mar14 and assisted on Phases 1 and 2 of the project. A project management unit was established in MEIDECC in Mar16 with the recruitment of a Project Manager. This was followed by the recruitment of Safeguards and Gender Specialist in Dec17, a Project Accountant in Jan19, and the O&amp;M consultant in Mar21. The 3 PMU staff resigned at various stages of the project and replacements were recruited.</narrative>
    </title>
